  "The socialist utopia of the future; the woman's argument in dialogue; the factory and the cooperative; the romance interrupted by politics; the direct, argumentative prose.",
  "The woman question, married disability, and the New Woman; wage labour, the strike, and the two nations; democracy, individualism, and the American experiment; the metropolis, the crowd, and the imperial capital.",
  "Gertrude Dix wrote The Image Breakers, one of the most explicitly socialist New Woman novels of the period: its vision of a socialist future and its argument about women's place in the movement make it a central text of the conjunction of feminism and socialism.",
  infl=["Olive Schreiner", "William Morris", "Edward Bellamy", "George Bernard Shaw", "Henrik Ibsen"],
